<?php
/**
 * Spartrak Utility Strip ("Top Container").
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: desktop node 595:14476, mobile node 724:25804.
 *
 * Two clusters, `justify-content: space-between`:
 *   notices (node 595:14494) — hotline label + number, shipping copy,
 *                              payment copy, separated by 4px dots
 *   options (node 595:14477) — track order / language / contact us
 *
 * CHILD ORDER is the reverse of Figma's LTR x-order, because these frames are
 * RTL-composed — see header.phtml's note. Concretely: `notices` is emitted
 * first so RTL places it at the inline start (Figma x=1048, the right), and
 * `options` last so it lands at the inline end (Figma x=16, the left). Within
 * `options` the same reversal puts "تتبع طلبك" nearest the start and "أتصل
 * بنا" furthest out, which is what the 1440 export shows.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * CONTENT COMES FROM CODE, NOT CMS BLOCKS
 * ===========================================================================
 * QA FIX (2026-08-25). The previous version pulled the hotline, shipping and
 * payment copy from five Magento\Cms\Block\Block children
 * (spartrak_support_*). Those static blocks were never created in the
 * database, so on the live site every one of them rendered EMPTY — which is
 * precisely why the strip looked nothing like Figma: the whole right-hand
 * cluster was simply missing.
 *
 * They are now plain __() strings, per the explicit project instruction that
 * this content is handled in code. That is also the better engineering
 * outcome here:
 *
 *   - It renders correctly on a fresh install with zero admin setup, so the
 *     header can never silently lose half its content again.
 *   - The copy stays changeable WITHOUT a deploy: __() strings are
 *     translatable, so Admin > Stores > Translations (or the theme's
 *     i18n/ar_EG.csv) still owns the wording per store view.
 *   - It removes five Magento\Cms\Block\Block instantiations, and their five
 *     static-block lookups, from EVERY page render — a real cost on a block
 *     that appears site-wide (CLAUDE.md §4).
 *
 * The Arabic copy is in this theme's i18n/ar_EG.csv, so the English store
 * view shows the source strings and the Arabic store view shows Figma's exact
 * wording.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE LANGUAGE SWITCHER
 * ===========================================================================
 * Figma places it here (node 595:14481: globe + store name + chevron), not in
 * the main navbar. It is rendered below as `store_language` — Porto's own,
 * already-working Magento\Store\Block\Switcher instance, RELOCATED into this
 * block by <move> in Smartwave_Porto/layout/default.xml.
 *
 * A <move> and not a new block declaration, deliberately: the 2026-08-24 pass
 * tried to satisfy this same requirement by declaring a SECOND
 * Magento\Store\Block\Switcher here, and it fatal-errored on every page even
 * after an explicit template prefix — the new instance kept resolving to
 * Magento_Store's core template, which calls $block->getViewModel() and was
 * never wired, instead of Porto's working override. Moving the existing
 * instance carries its own template resolution with it, so there is nothing
 * to re-resolve and nothing to crash.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHAT FIGMA DOES *NOT* PUT IN THIS STRIP — flagged, not silently dropped
 * ===========================================================================
 * WhatsApp and Branches appear nowhere in Figma's header, desktop or mobile,
 * so they are not rendered here. Both remain reachable site-wide from the
 * footer, and "أتصل بنا" here links to the real contact route. This does
 * narrow ia-and-flows.md's "support actions visible everywhere" from the
 * header to the footer; called out for a decision rather than settled here.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */
$contactUsUrl = $block->getUrl('contact/index/index');
/**
 * "تتبع طلبك" goes to the shopper's OWN order list, never to Magento's guest
 * lookup form.
 *
 * It used to point at sales/guest/form — the "Orders and Returns" screen that
 * asks for an order id, a billing surname and an email before it will show
 * anything. A signed-in shopper was being asked to re-key facts the store
 * already holds about them, on an untranslated core form, to reach a page they
 * were already entitled to.
 *
 * ONE URL FOR EVERYONE, because this block is full-page cached and there is a
 * further HTTP cache in front of Magento (see account-chip.phtml): an href
 * chosen from PHP session state would be served to the wrong visitor. The route
 * itself resolves the two cases at request time instead —
 * Spartrak\CustomerAccount\Plugin\Sales\PromptSignInForGuest sends a guest back
 * with the sign-in modal open and `next=orders`, so signing in completes the
 * journey rather than ending it.
 *
 * `data-auth-guest` on the anchor lets js/spartrak-auth.js skip that round trip
 * when it can already see the visitor is a guest. It is an optimisation over a
 * correct server behaviour, not the behaviour itself.
 */
$trackOrderUrl = $block->getUrl('sales/order/history');
$languageSwitcher = $block->getChildHtml('store_language');
?>
<div class="spartrak-support-strip" role="complementary" aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Store information')) ?>">
    <div class="spartrak-support-strip__inner">
        <div class="spartrak-support-strip__notices">
            <?php /* Figma node 595:14494. Order here is RTL reading order:
                     hotline label, its number, shipping, payment — with a 4px
                     dot between consecutive items. */ ?>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__notice"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Hotline')) ?></span>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__separator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <?php /* The number is Latin-script inside an RTL block, so it is
                     bidi-isolated in CSS (see _support-strip.less) to stop
                     "12384" reordering. */ ?>
            <a class="spartrak-support-strip__notice spartrak-support-strip__notice--hotline-value"
               href="tel:<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('12384')) ?>"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('12384')) ?></a>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__separator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__notice spartrak-support-strip__notice--marketing">
                <?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Fast delivery nationwide')) ?>
            </span>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__separator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="spartrak-support-strip__notice spartrak-support-strip__notice--marketing">
                <?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Secure payment options')) ?>
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-support-strip__options">
            <?php /* Node 595:14486 — icon leads the label (Figma x: label 0,
                     icon 56 in LTR order, so the icon trails there and leads
                     once reversed for RTL). */ ?>
            <a class="spartrak-support-strip__item"
               href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($trackOrderUrl) ?>"
               data-auth-open
               data-auth-guest
               data-auth-next="orders">
                <span class="spartrak-support-strip__icon--track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Track your order')) ?></span>
            </a>

            <?php if (trim($languageSwitcher)) : ?>
                <?= /* @noEscape */ $languageSwitcher ?>
            <?php endif; ?>

            <?php /* Node 595:14478 — label only, no icon in Figma. Mobile
                     (node 724:25805) drops this item entirely; hidden by CSS
                     rather than by a viewport check in PHP, because this block
                     is full-page-cached and cannot branch on device. */ ?>
            <?php /* PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT, NOT A REPLACEMENT. The href stays
                     the real /contact/ URL — it is what a shopper without
                     JavaScript follows, and what a middle-click or a "copy link"
                     yields — while js/spartrak-dialog.js upgrades the click into
                     opening the contact dialog in place. The route itself is
                     intercepted server-side by
                     Spartrak\Contact\Observer\RedirectContactPageToDialog, so
                     even the un-upgraded path ends at the dialog rather than at
                     Magento's contact form. */ ?>
            <a class="spartrak-support-strip__item spartrak-support-strip__item--contact"
               href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($contactUsUrl) ?>"
               data-spartrak-dialog-open="contact">
                <span><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Contact us')) ?></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
